      <data key="d6">cb-0457</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;POLICE-COMMUNITY RELATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;OPIOID EPIDEMIC&quot;">
      <data key="d3">12.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Both issues, police-community relations and the opioid epidemic, are challenges that need to be addressed, suggesting they are part of a broader context of social and public health concerns."</data>
      <data key="d5">"social issues, public health"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0457</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;POLICE-COMMUNITY RELATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;NEW STRATEGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"New strategies also aim to address police-community relations, indicating a broad approach to multiple issues."</data>
      <data key="d5">"community engagement, strategy"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0457</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;OPIOID EPIDEMIC&quot;" target="&quot;NEW STRATEGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"New strategies are specifically aimed at combating the opioid epidemic, indicating a direct focus on this event."</data>
      <data key="d5">"epidemic response, strategy"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0457</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NEW STRATEGIES&quot;" target="&quot;ADDRESSING CONCERNS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Addressing concerns involves implementing new strategies, indicating a direct link between the need to address issues and the methods to do so."</data>
